<article class="env-lemma" id="0B8P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B8P">Lemma <span data-tag="0B8P">18.32.3</span>.</a> Let $f : (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}) \to (\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}), \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D})$ be a morphism of ringed topoi. The pullback $f^*\mathcal{L}$ of an invertible $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$-module is invertible. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0B8N" data-tag="0B8N">18.32.2</a> there exists an $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$-module $\mathcal{N}$ such that $\mathcal{L} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}} \mathcal{N} \cong \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {D}$. Pulling back we get $f^*\mathcal{L} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}} f^*\mathcal{N} \cong \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/03EL" data-tag="03EL">18.26.2</a>. Thus $f^*\mathcal{L}$ is invertible by Lemma <a href="/tag/0B8N" data-tag="0B8N">18.32.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>